# SYNCED FROM AI-Handbook — do not edit in a consumer repo. Local edits are overwritten by the next sync and their reasoning is lost; change the handbook instead.
# Dispatch receipts, and every one of them is EVIDENCE rather than a decision.
#
# One file describes one dispatch at one moment: which role ran, on which
# model, against which head, and what it answered. It is worthless once the
# moment passes and re-derivable by dispatching again, so it is session-local
# and never repo history.
#
# THE COMMITTED HALF IS GONE (#89 cut, 2026-09-16). This directory used to
# hold two kinds, split by that line: evidence ignored here, and DECISIONS --
# review-loop budgets and their extension grants -- committed beside them so a
# spent allowance survived the container. Budgets, extensions, round counts and
# readiness receipts were all removed with the accounting machinery that read
# them. Nothing in this directory is committed now, which is why the patterns
# below are a single glob rather than the named-shape list they replace.
#
# Named by prefix rather than ignoring the directory outright, so this README
# and this file stay tracked: git cannot re-include a file whose parent
# directory is excluded, and written that way the negations read correctly and
# do nothing.
#
# This lives in the directory it governs rather than in the repo root so that
# it is an ordinary synced file — one copy in the handbook, carried to every
# consumer. Patterns are relative to this directory.
fable-*.json
